  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.repositories.mock.MockCatalogItemsRepository\": {\n        \"summary\": \"An in-memory mock repository implementation for catalog items, designed for testing the API surface area. Implements CatalogItemsRepository and TestPath interfaces to provide CRUD operations on catalog items stored in an ArrayList. The constructor pre-populates the catalog with three brake-related products (brake pads, calipers, and guide pins). Key methods include: getCatalogItems() - retrieves all catalog items as defensive copies; getCatalogItem(String sku) - fetches a specific item by SKU using case-insensitive matching; upsertCatalogItem(String sku, CatalogItem catalogItem, String eTag) - inserts or updates items, returning true for updates and false for inserts; removeCatalogItem(String sku, String eTag) - deletes items by SKU, returning true if found; reset() - clears the catalog for test cleanup. The implementation uses a private compareSkuNumbers() helper for case-insensitive SKU comparison and returns defensive copies to prevent external modification. The eTag parameter is accepted but not utilized in this mock implementation.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/repositories/mock/MockCatalogItemsRepository.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
